    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0218" n="184" xml:id="pg184"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron von Thielmann to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s note of
                    to-day’s date, No. 301, I beg to say that I shall thank you for kindly
                    instructing, by telegraph, the United States consul at St. Pierre, Martinique,
                    to extend his protection and render assistance to Captain Aim, master of the
                    German bark <hi rendition="#italic">Elisabeth Ahrens.</hi></p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thielmann.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
